{"OptimizedCursorPaginator.get_result passes negative cursor.offset directly to Django queryset slicing when enable_advanced_features=True, causing AssertionError: Negative indexing is not supported": 0.9663973450660706, "BasePaginator.get_result skips the max(0, ...) clamp when cursor.is_prev is True, allowing crafted cursors with negative offsets to pass negative values to Django queryset slicing": 0.8869824409484863, "OptimizedCursorPaginator.get_item_key applies math.floor/ceil to the field value, which will raise TypeError for datetime values when used with order_by='-datetime' in OrganizationAuditLogsEndpoint": 0.9883031249046326, "OrganizationAuditLogsEndpoint dereferences organization_context.member.has_global_access without guarding for member being None, which can raise AttributeError and return a 500": 0.8910008072853088, "Span buffering switches span-buf:s:* keys from Redis Sets to Sorted Sets (zadd/zscan/zunionstore) with no migration/backward-compatibility path, so existing set-typed keys can cause Redis WRONGTYPE errors": 0.9495010375976562, "SpansBuffer._load_segment_data no longer enforces max_segment_spans, so segments can contain far more spans than intended, increasing flush CPU/memory and risking timeouts": 0.9840510487556458, "The Lua script evicts spans via zpopmin when a segment exceeds 1000 spans with no logging, metrics, or return-value indicating eviction occurred, creating silent data loss with zero observability": 0.9388366937637329, "The _load_segment_data method no longer checks max_segment_spans during segment loading, leaving no Python-side protection against oversized segments during flush under concurrent writes": 0.958294689655304, "The Lua redirect-resolution loop limit is reduced from 10000 to 1000, increasing the likelihood that deep redirect chains will not fully resolve and leaving spans merged into incorrect segment keys": 0.8964706063270569}